    "updated_at": "2022-10-17T22:17:50Z",
    "body": "\"Valid\" here will need to be defined as the spec defines a clear notion of a \"validation error\". Specifically, a URL can parse successfully but still be considered \"invalid\" per the spec. Does \"isValid(...) === true\" mean that the URL parses successfully or does it mean it parsed without any validation errors?",
