    "updated_at": "2022-11-07T09:03:24Z",
    "body": "See also #372 although that would not return a boolean presumably.\r\n\r\nGiven that there's popular libraries that do something like this this is worth doing I think, but this is not validation. We should either call this something like `canParse` and return a boolean or `parse` and return null or a `URL` object.",
