    "created_at": "2022-11-07T09:10:58Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-11-07T09:10:58Z",
    "body": "It's not clear to me solving this at the level of a new API is the best idea. Wouldn't it be better to make `try / catch` faster? In particular, if you use `catch { }` instead of `catch (e) { }`, that should be a reliable signal to the engine that there's no need to construct a stack, which is apparently expensive (benchmarks pending).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
