    "updated_at": "2022-11-08T02:30:52Z",
    "body": "For the ergonomics of try/catch, perhaps that's something that should be solved at the language level? For instance, some languages have a `try?` feature which returns nil on error. Would this be useful for other, non-URL APIs?",
