    "created_at": "2023-03-06T06:34:47Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-03-06T07:07:02Z",
    "body": "I'm not convinced that `canParse()` is the check that the people using those libraries really want. For example, we can parse `a::<!>::` as a URL, but you probably wouldn't want to accept that in an input field.\r\n\r\nIn the absence of benchmarks I'm also not convinced by the performance argument.\r\n\r\n*Edit:* Actually, even if there were benchmarks, why do we think this is performance critical? Who needs to verify whether a million URLs parse anyway?",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
