    "created_at": "2024-04-17T12:00:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-04-17T12:05:14Z",
    "body": "If you have the following code, the url actually needs to be parsed twice.\r\n\r\n```js\r\nconst url = 'http://foo.com'\r\nlet parsed_url = null\r\nif (URL.canParse(url)) {\r\n  parsed_url = new URL(url)\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nLooking back, now that we've added `URL.parse()` to return null if it's invalid(https://github.com/whatwg/url/pull/825), why do we need `URL.canParse()`?",
    "author_association": "NONE",
